<task id="243" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>BFF: Document Intelligence extraction via the stamp's managed identity (owner D13, plan G17) — "key OR managed identity" in both TextExtractorService guards, then remove `DocumentIntelligence-ApiKey` from the catalog and `customer.bicep`</title>
    <phase>Model 1 dedicated-stamp remediation — plan §7 T243 (owner decision D13 keyless stamps, gap G17)</phase>
    <gate>startable now (T226 done); independent of T248 (owner-blocked)</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies BFF `.cs` (tag bff-api) + its unit tests, `customer.bicep` (deployed by H2a) and the canonical secret catalog.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Small, fully specified change on an existing credential-selection pattern; the risk is completeness (catalog regeneration, BFF §10 obligations), not judgment.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>touches .claude/CHANGELOG.md (main-session-only) and the BFF hot path</parallel-reason>
    <tags>bff-api, ai, document-intelligence, auth, provisioning, bicep, canonical-secret-catalog, testing, model1-dedicated</tags>
    <deps>226</deps>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Let the BFF extract text and layout with Document Intelligence through its managed identity when no API key is
    configured, then stop writing the Document Intelligence key into customer stamps.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer (.NET 10 BFF, Bicep, canonical secret catalog). Follow ADRs and BFF §10 strictly.
  </role>

  <goal>
    On a customer stamp with no `DocumentIntelligence__DocIntelKey`, `TextExtractorService` text and layout extraction
    reach Document Intelligence through the stamp UAMI (`CreateDocIntelClient`'s existing managed-identity branch);
    environments that still configure the key keep using it. No customer stamp writes or references
    `DocumentIntelligence-ApiKey` any more.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Owner D13 (2026-09-30): keyless customer stamps; BFF changes follow "key if configured, else MI" so the shared dev
      env keeps working. Plan G17: both extraction paths gate on `DocIntelKey` (`TextExtractorService.cs:743` text,
      `:967` layout), so the managed-identity client in `CreateDocIntelClient` (`:76-98`, auth-v4 task 054) is never
      reached. The credential is already injected: `TextExtractorService` takes an optional `TokenCredential`, and the BFF
      registers the UAMI-pinned `TokenCredential` singleton (`AnalysisServicesModule.cs:181` builds the service through
      DI). The stamp side is ready: `modules/doc-intelligence.bicep` sets `customSubDomainName` (Entra needs a custom
      subdomain — the shared dev account `spaarke-docintel-dev` has none, which is why dev keeps its key) and grants the
      stamp UAMI Cognitive Services User. `customer.bicep` still writes the key (`kvSecrets` `DocumentIntelligence-ApiKey`,
      from the module's `listKeys` output) and H4b emits `DocumentIntelligence__DocIntelKey` from the catalog
      (`scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml:369`, marked INTERIM until T243).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/TextExtractorService.cs (guards :743, :967; CreateDocIntelClient :76)</file>
      <file>tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Ai/TextExtractorServiceTests.cs (configuration tests ~:125-210)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Configuration/DocumentIntelligenceOptions.cs (DocIntelKey doc comment)</file>
      <file>scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml (DocumentIntelligence-ApiKey entry) + Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1 (regenerate generated/)</file>
      <file>infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep (kvSecrets map, comments ~:606-616, ~:740-756) + customer.json</file>
      <file>infrastructure/bicep/modules/doc-intelligence.bicep (`docIntelligenceKey` listKeys output)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
