  </knowledge>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner D13">
      "Key if configured, else managed identity": when `DocIntelKey` is set the key path is used exactly as today. The
      guards require the endpoint plus a credential — the key OR the injected `TokenCredential`. Do not delete the key
      fallback (that is the shared dev/demo follow-on, plan §6).
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="plan T244 (scope boundary)">
      Do NOT set `disableLocalAuth` on the Document Intelligence account (T244 owns local-auth disabling for every
      stamp resource). Do not change OpenAI, AI Search, Redis or Content Safety.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10 BFF hygiene">
      Modification of an existing service only — no new endpoint, service, DI registration or package. State the placement
      (existing service, in BFF) in the notes; measure publish size against a FRESH master build from short-path
      worktrees with `Compress-Archive` (report both absolute sizes, delta and file counts); confirm no new HIGH CVE.
      Update `TextExtractorServiceTests` for the changed behaviour.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="KV credential lifecycle (provisioning.md)">
      Removing the catalog entry stops NEW stamps from receiving the key. Do not delete any existing vault secret
      (dev/demo `ai-docintel-key` stay); no live Azure change in this task.
    </constraint>
  </constraints>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>The BFF's DI does not pass the `TokenCredential` to `TextExtractorService` (the optional parameter is null at runtime) → STOP and report; do not add a registration without saying so.</trigger>
    <trigger>Any consumer other than the BFF's `DocumentIntelligence:DocIntelKey` (H13 probe, script, test, Bicep output reader) depends on `DocumentIntelligence-ApiKey` or the `docIntelligenceKey` output → STOP and report it before removing.</trigger>
    <trigger>Publish-size delta ≥ +5 MB, or file counts differ between the two publishes → STOP (CLAUDE.md §10).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Guards at `:743` and `:967`: configured = endpoint AND (key OR credential). Update the "not configured" messages to name both options.</step>
    <step order="2">Tests: managed-identity path passes the guard (endpoint + no key + a fake `TokenCredential` → reaches the next check, e.g. file-size limit, without a network call) for text AND layout; endpoint + no key + no credential → "not configured" (rename the existing key-missing test accordingly).</step>
    <step order="3">Catalog: remove `DocumentIntelligence-ApiKey` from `manifest.yaml`; regenerate `generated/` with the generator; `-Verify`.</step>
    <step order="4">`customer.bicep`: drop the kvSecrets entry and fix the comments; `modules/doc-intelligence.bicep`: drop the `listKeys` output (no consumer left). Recompile `customer.json` (`--outfile`).</step>
    <step order="5">Docs: deployment guide / inventory / any current doc that says stamps carry the Doc Intel key; `DocumentIntelligenceOptions.DocIntelKey` doc comment ("optional — managed identity when unset"); CHANGELOG entry if `.claude` changes.</step>
    <step order="6">BFF §10: publish-size vs fresh master (short paths), CVE check, placement statement.</step>
    <step order="7">Verify + Step 9.5 + close (POML notes, TASK-INDEX, plan §7 T243 + G17, current-task, drift check) + commit + push.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="file-modified">TextExtractorService.cs; TextExtractorServiceTests.cs; DocumentIntelligenceOptions.cs (comment); manifest.yaml + generated/; customer.bicep + customer.json; modules/doc-intelligence.bicep; docs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Text and layout extraction with endpoint + injected credential and NO key pass the configuration guard (test reaches the next check without a network call).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Endpoint + no key + no credential → both paths return the "not configured" failure; endpoint missing → "not configured" (unchanged); endpoint + key → key path unchanged (existing tests pass).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`git grep DocumentIntelligence-ApiKey` outside historical notes/CHANGELOG returns nothing in the catalog, generated files, `customer.bicep`/`customer.json`; `docIntelligenceKey` output gone; catalog `-Verify` OK; checked-in `customer.json` = fresh compile; `bicep-e2e-dry-run.ps1` PASS.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF builds 0 errors; `Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests` TextExtractorService tests pass and the full BFF unit suite has no new failures vs master; ControlPlane.Tests no failures beyond the 6 T221 baseline; ArchTests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish size: master vs branch from fresh short-path worktrees, `Compress-Archive`, both sizes + delta + equal file counts recorded in the notes; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: the two configuration branches above for text and layout; anything beyond needs a one-line justification in the notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Filed 2026-10-02 (SESSION 31) from plan §7 T243 after T249 closed; T248 is owner-blocked, T243 is next in order.

    COMPLETION (2026-10-02). Verified: BFF builds 0 warnings 0 errors; BFF unit suite 13,575 pass / 0 fail / 54 skip of
    13,629 (full run before the credential-rejection catch was added; TextExtractorServiceTests + ComposePdfIntakeSourceTests
    re-run after it: 87/87); ControlPlane.Tests 2127 pass / 6 fail (T221 CustomerRunGuardModulePostConfigureTests baseline) /
    1 skip; ArchTests 341/341; catalog -Verify OK; customer.json = fresh compile; bicep-e2e-dry-run PASS; prereqs OK;
    task-status drift clean.

    DONE: TextExtractorService — `IsDocIntelConfigured` = endpoint AND (key OR injected TokenCredential) gates text and
    layout; CreateDocIntelClient unchanged (key wins when set — dev/demo keep theirs, D13); a rejected credential (401/403
    or AuthenticationFailedException) returns a plain "rejected the service's credential" failure and does not trip the
    circuit breaker (code-review W6); the managed-identity notice logs once per process (adr W4). DI already passes the
    UAMI-pinned TokenCredential (Program.cs:48 → optional ctor param) — escalation trigger #1 did not fire. Catalog:
    `DocumentIntelligence-ApiKey` removed (+ generated/); customer.bicep stops writing it; doc-intelligence.bicep's
    `listKeys` output removed (its only consumer was customer.bicep — trigger #2 did not fire). `disableLocalAuth` left to
    T244 (boundary kept). Docs: DocIntelKey option comment, appsettings.template `_DocIntelKey_comment`,
    CONFIGURATION-MATRIX (DocIntelKey optional; DocumentIntelligence:Enabled is FALSE when unset), ai-document-summary,
    inventory, spec ADR-028 tension row, .claude pattern + CHANGELOG.

    SCOPE EXPANSION (owner D22, AskUserQuestion 2026-10-02): FOUND that no stamp ever set the BFF's AI master switch —
    the DI gates read GetValue<bool>("DocumentIntelligence:Enabled") (false when unset; the options-class default true
    does not apply), so stamps registered NullTextExtractor and ran without analysis/playbooks/search (the 2026-08-22
    stand-up log). Added the catalog per-env literal `DocumentIntelligence__Enabled=true` (plan G29 ✅). It exposes AI Search
    MI 403 until T244 and the BFF's hard-coded dev Content Safety fallback until T246 → owner: keep it, T244 + T246 are
    hard prerequisites of T186 (recorded in the plan + T186 deps). Startup impact (code-review): no new fail-fast; two more
    KV references (AzureOpenAI-Endpoint, AiSearch-Endpoint) must resolve at boot because the indexing worker builds its
    clients — proven at T186.

    BFF §10: PLACEMENT — modification of an existing BFF service (TextExtractorService, Services/Ai) only; no endpoint,
    service, DI registration or package. PUBLISH SIZE (fresh short-path worktrees, `dotnet publish -c Release`,
    PowerShell Compress-Archive, incl. PDBs): master 818840ac6 = 45.66 MB / 212 files; pre-T243 33365edd2 = 45.54 MB /
    212 files; T243 = 45.54 MB / 212 files → delta +0.00 MB (branch −0.12 MB vs master = master's growth since the last
    merge). CVE: `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — none; csproj unchanged.

